      ":question/problem": "Consider the system ${x}^{\u2032}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $\u03a6(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $\u03a6(t)$ satisfies the matrix differential equation ${\u03a6}^{\u2032}(t)=A\\,\u03a6(t)$ is given below.\n\n*Hint: $[a,\\,b]$ denotes a matrix whose columns are vectors $a$ and $b.$*\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $\u03a6(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}^{\u2032}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${x}_{2}^{\u2032}(t)=A{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${\u03a6}^{\u2032}(t)=[{x}_{1}^{\u2032}(t),\\,{x}_{2}^{\u2032}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ ${\u03a6}^{\u2032}(t)=[A{x}_{1}(t),\\,A{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${\u03a6}^{\u2032}(t)=A[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${\u03a6}^{\u2032}(t)=A\u03a6(t)$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from the fact that {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L4}$ and substitution from lines {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ and substitution from line {{field-3}}."
